docs {
  # Settlements


  All routes require Bearer authentication, an ACTIVE account and ACTIVE membership with left_at=null. Membership IDs belong to this group; user IDs are not interchangeable with them. An owner or site ADMIN has no special payment permissions.

  Group status enum: `ACTIVE`, `SETTLING`, `CLOSED`. Both ACTIVE and SETTLING allow settlement writes; CLOSED allows reads only. Expenses, polls and draws remain frozen whenever the group is not ACTIVE.

  Payment status enum (uppercase, case-sensitive): `PENDING`, `SUCCESS`, `REJECT`, `CANCELED`. PENDING and CANCELED are visible only to their active sender/recipient. SUCCESS and REJECT, including receipts, are visible to every active group member. Filtered list counts follow the same visibility rules.

  Payments cannot be edited. Only the active sender may soft-delete PENDING. Only the active recipient may confirm/reject PENDING. Confirmation records a successful external payment; this endpoint does not perform a bank transfer. Rejection/cancellation never count as successful payments. Owner/admin cannot override either party.

  A sender who leaves loses access; their existing PENDING payment remains answerable by its active recipient. If the recipient leaves/is removed before responding, incoming PENDING payments become CANCELED atomically with `cancel_reason=RECIPIENT_LEFT`. Rejoining does not revive them. Former-member financial relationships are outside the active-member balance calculation; history remains stored. `is_external` is true when either party currently has inactive membership/left_at. Membership status values remain ACTIVE/INACTIVE.

  IDs are manual environment variables. No response script sets or overwrites settlement IDs. Set settlementGroupId, settlementToMemberId (from Get Group Members), settlementId, and settlementAttachmentIds yourself. Auth login/refresh keeps its existing token behavior.


  ## Manual test flow

  1. Apply migrations, start services/app and log in as sender A. Obtain recipient B member_id from Get Group Members.
  2. Set settlementGroupId, settlementToMemberId and settlementAmountToman. Optional: upload receipt, copy its ID into settlementAttachmentIds=[ID].
  3. Create Settlement, copy data.id into settlementId yourself. Check A outgoing and B incoming lists in separate Bruno/Postman sessions.
  4. Check C/owner cannot see this pending record or its receipt. B can confirm or reject; only A can delete while pending.
  5. Confirm one payment, reject a second, delete a third. Confirm/reject history and receipts become visible to C; deleted records disappear. No final record can be edited/deleted.
  6. Try a sender leaving after Create: B can still confirm. Try recipient leaving/removal: payment becomes CANCELED, cancel_reason=RECIPIENT_LEFT, even if B later rejoins.
  7. Move group ACTIVE -> SETTLING: settlement writes still work, expense/poll/draw writes stop. Resolve all pending payments, then move SETTLING -> CLOSED: all settlement writes stop. Reopening is not supported by this workflow.

  ## Receipt privacy

  SETTLEMENT_RECEIPT is always private. Metadata, streaming download, signed URL batches, ZIP downloads and group attachment lists enforce the same visibility. Linking happens only through Create Settlement; do not send settlement_id or expense_id when uploading/confirming a receipt. Once linked, direct deletion is blocked with 409 SETTLEMENT_RECEIPT_LOCKED, including for its uploader/owner. Delete a pending payment first to detach its files.

  Receipt signed download URLs expire after the configured presigned TTL (currently 15 minutes). Previously issued signed URLs cannot be revoked instantly. Presigned PUT uploads are copied to a fresh server-controlled object on confirmation; subsequent PUTs to the original upload URL do not change the confirmed receipt.

  ## Group lifecycle

  PATCH /api/v1/groups/:groupID/status accepts ACTIVE, SETTLING, CLOSED. Only owner/site-admin may manage the group lifecycle (this does not grant payment permissions). Forward transitions are ACTIVE -> SETTLING -> CLOSED. POST /groups/:groupID/archive remains an alias for moving to SETTLING. Existing INACTIVE group rows migrate to SETTLING; membership ACTIVE/INACTIVE and poll ACTIVE/INACTIVE enums are unchanged. Closing with a pending payment returns 409 GROUP_PENDING_SETTLEMENTS. A group with non-deleted payment history cannot be deleted (409 GROUP_HAS_SETTLEMENTS).

  ## Scope

  This feature records external payments and decisions. It does not send money, charge wallets, schedule notifications or expose debt graph/report endpoints. Current balances are calculated only for the creation warning. Final SUCCESS records remain the source for future balance/report calculations.
}
